            {
              "text": "In Sydney’s prestige real estate market, **the individual lead agent is often more important than the agency brand**. A $10M sale requires access to off-market buyer pools, discreet negotiation skills, and high-net-worth (HNW) buyer relationships. \n\nThe top agencies and boutique powerhouses with the strongest track records in the $10M+ segment depend on the property's location and architectural style:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Global Brands & Ultra-Prestige Specialists\nThese agencies are best if your property appeals to international buyers, foreign capital, or expats:\n\n* **Sydney Sotheby’s International Realty (Double Bay)**\n  * **Key Agents:** Michael Pallier, Clint Ballard.\n  * **Track Record:** Michael Pallier is one of the highest-grossing agents in Australian history, regularly closing multi-million-dollar waterfronts and estates in Vaucluse, Rose Bay, and Point Piper. \n  * **Best For:** Harborfronts, large trophy estates, and properties requiring exposure to buyers from mainland China, Singapore, the US, and the UK.\n* **Private Property Global / Forbes Global Properties**\n  * **Key Agent:** Ken Jacobs.\n  * **Track Record:** Ken Jacobs has set Australian national price records (brokering historic Point Piper estates like *Fairwater* and *Elaine*).\n  * **Best For:** Ultra-discreet, private sales of architectural or heritage significance.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Eastern Suburbs Prestige Powerhouses\nFor harbor-side enclaves (Vaucluse, Bellevue Hill, Double Bay, Darling Point) or coastal belts (Bronte, Tamarama, Bondi):\n\n* **Highland Double Bay**\n  * **Key Agents:** Bill Malouf, David Malouf.\n  * **Track Record:** Decades at the pinnacle of Eastern Suburbs luxury. They have an extensive direct Rolodex of Australian business leaders and high-net-worth families.\n* **The Agency**\n  * **Key Agent:** Ben Collier.\n  * **Track Record:** Consistently ranked among the top residential agents in Australia. Collier dominates sales above $10M across Woollahra, Paddington, Centennial Park, and Bellevue Hill.\n  * **Best For:** High-end grand terraces, parkside estates, and luxury character homes.\n* **Ray White Double Bay**\n  * **Key Agents:** Elliott Placks, Ashley Bierman.\n  * **Track Record:** High-volume prestige market share in the East. They have deep access to active local finance, tech, and legal buyers and run competitive, highly visible auction and private treaty campaigns.\n* **Pillinger**\n  * **Key Agent:** Brad Pillinger.\n  * **Track Record:** An independent boutique agency that focuses almost entirely on the $10M–$50M+ trophy market in Point Piper, Bellevue Hill, and Vaucluse.\n* **TRG (The Rubinstein Group)**\n  * **Key Agent:** Gavin Rubinstein.\n  * **Track Record:** Known for aggressive marketing campaigns, high digital reach, and strong clearance rates across Rose Bay, Dover Heights, Vaucluse, and Woollahra.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Lower North Shore Specialists\nFor properties in Mosman, Clifton Gardens, Balmoral, Cremorne Point, or Neutral Bay:\n\n* **Simeon Partners:** Led by Richard Simeon, renowned for setting price-per-square-metre records in Balmoral and Mosman waterfronts.\n* **Atlas by LJ Hooker:** Michael Coombs is one of the Lower North Shore's top-performing prestige agents for $10M+ harborfront homes.\n* **Ray White Lower North Shore:** Geoff Smith and Richard Harding hold significant market share for prestige family homes in Mosman and surrounds.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Inner-East & Design-Led Prestige\n* **BresicWhitney (Darlinghurst / Inner East)**\n  * **Key Agents:** Shannan Whitney, Maclay Longhurst.\n  * **Best For:** Architectural masterworks, high-end conversions, and trophy terraces in Paddington, Woollahra, Darlinghurst, and Centennial Park.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Selection Criteria for a $10M Listing\n\n1. **Off-Market Network:** Many properties in this bracket transact off-market. Ask the agent: *\"How many qualified buyers in this price bracket do you currently have registered who missed out on your last three sales?\"*\n2. **Local Street-by-Street Comps:** A Lower North Shore agent will rarely perform as well in Woollahra as a local specialist, and vice versa. Prioritize agents who have transacted $8M–$15M properties within a 2 km radius in the past 12 months.\n3. **Co-Agent Consideration:** It is common in Sydney’s $10M+ market to appoint joint exclusive agencies (e.g., pairing a hyper-local boutique specialist like Pillinger or The Agency with an international-reach network like Sotheby's).",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
